---
// Policy text is reproduced verbatim from the previous site
// (beardgroup.com/BeardGroupPrivacyPolicy.htm), including its "as of" date.
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const sections = [
  { id: 'nutshell', title: 'In a Nutshell' },
  { id: 'when-you-visit', title: 'When you visit us' },
  { id: 'when-you-use-a-feature', title: 'When you use a feature of our Web site' },
  { id: 'protecting-information', title: 'How we protect and share the personally identifying information' },
  { id: 'contacting-you', title: 'When we will contact you' },
  { id: 'cookies', title: 'Cookies' },
  { id: 'sale-or-closure', title: 'If Beard Group is sold or goes out of business' },
  { id: 'changes', title: 'Changes to this Privacy Policy' },
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="The Beard Group, Inc. Privacy Policy.">
  <PageHero title="Privacy Policy" lede="As of August 25, 2017" />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container policy-layout">
      <nav class="toc" aria-labelledby="toc-heading">
        <p id="toc-heading" class="eyebrow">On this page</p>
        <ol>
          {
            sections.map((section) => (
              <li>
                <a href={`#${section.id}`}>{section.title}</a>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <article class="policy">
        <p class="policy__intro">
          Beard Group, Inc., takes your privacy very seriously. This Privacy Policy tells you what your
          rights are, and the rules we follow to protect your personal information. Please take a moment
          to read through it, so you understand what information we collect, and how we might use it.
          Peter A. Chapman is our designated privacy officer. You can reach Mr. Chapman by e-mail at <a
            href="mailto:peter@beardgroup.com">peter@beardgroup.com</a
          > or by telephone at <a href="tel:+12159457000">(215) 945-7000</a>, and he would be delighted
          to hear from you if you have any questions or need any additional information.
        </p>

        <section class="policy__summary" aria-labelledby="nutshell">
          <h2 id="nutshell">In a Nutshell:</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>We only collect your personal information when we think we need it.</li>
            <li>
              We may use Internet cookies to learn more about our visitors, and what they do on our Web
              site.
            </li>
            <li>
              We don't sell or share your personal information with anyone, except when required by law,
              to improve our products or services, or protect our rights, but we might choose to in the
              future.
            </li>
            <li>
              We only store your information when we think it's needed for us to operate this Web site
              and its features.
            </li>
            <li>We may change our Privacy Policy from time to time.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <h2 id="when-you-visit">When you visit us:</h2>

        <h3>What we collect</h3>
        <p>
          We may collect some information about you when you visit our site. This information does not
          identify you. For example, it may include what web browser you use, your preferred language,
          and when you visited the site. This is commonly called non-identifying information.
        </p>

        <h3>How we use the information</h3>
        <p>
          We use non-identifying information to understand how our visitors use our Web site, so that
          we can make it even better. We also use it to track things like user trends and behavior on
          our Web site. From time-to-time, we may create a report that is made public based on
          non-identifying information. For example, we may do this to show user trends on our Web site.
        </p>

        <h3>Sharing the information</h3>
        <p>
          We may also share this information with third parties (including select vendors, customers,
          partners and affiliated entities). This report probably won't include information that
          personally identifies you, but it might. It will include the non-identifying information we
          collected when you used our site.
        </p>

        <h2 id="when-you-use-a-feature">When you use a feature of our Web site:</h2>

        <h3>What we collect</h3>
        <p>
          If you decide to use some features of our Web site, you may be asked to give us personally
          identifying information. For example, if you sign up for our mailing list, you will need to
          give us your name and e-mail address. We only collect information that is necessary. For
          example, we don't ask for your age when you send us a message through our Web site.
        </p>

        <h3>Refusing to share information</h3>
        <p>
          You always have the option to refuse to give personal information. But, if you don't share the
          necessary personal information, you might not be able to use certain features of our Web site.
          For example, you won't be able to send us an e-mail message, subscribe to <i
            >Turnarounds &amp; Workouts</i
          >, or learn about any of our other products without giving us your e-mail address and name.
        </p>

        <h3>When we share the information</h3>
        <p>
          We don't ordinarily sell or share personally identifying information with anyone, unless
          required by law, required to provide services you requested, or if we are acquired by another
          company (more on this below), but we might, by accident or by design.
        </p>

        <h2 id="protecting-information">
          How we protect and share the personally identifying information:
        </h2>

        <h3>Protecting the information</h3>
        <p>
          We protect personally identifying information by using reasonable measures to prevent the
          unauthorized use, access, alteration, or destruction of the information, with the same level
          of care and prudence with which we safeguard all of our assets.
        </p>

        <h3>Sharing the information</h3>
        <p>
          We don't ordinarily sell or rent personally identifying information to anyone. But we might at
          some point in the future. For information that is or may be personally identifying, we only
          share it with employees, contractors, or other organizations that need to know the information
          to provide services or process it, and have agreed not to share the information with others.
          That too might change in the future. We will share the information (only to the extent
          necessary) if we are asked by a court or other governmental agency for the information, or we
          believe it is reasonably necessary to share the information to protect us, third parties, or the
          general public.
        </p>

        <h2 id="contacting-you">When we will contact you:</h2>
        <p>
          If you supply us with your e-mail address, we may send you occasional e-mail messages about
          other products and services we sell or to get feedback from you. You can unsubscribe from these
          additional electronic mailings at any time by contacting us, and we'll do our best to stop the
          flow of unwanted information.
        </p>

        <h2 id="cookies">Cookies:</h2>
        <p>
          A cookie is a small piece of data that a Web site stores on your computer when you visit. Your
          computer will then give that cookie to the Web site each time you return for a visit. Cookies
          can be used for many things. We may use cookies to help us understand how and when visitors use
          our site, your Web site preferences, and a little bit about who you are, to the extent a cookie
          can reveal that information. For example, we may learn what country you come from, that you read
          Web sites in English, and that you use a Macbook or PC. We may also do this through the use of
          cookies from third-party sites, like Google Analytics.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you don't want cookies to be saved to your computer, you can change your browser settings to
          refuse cookies. But, keep in mind that you may not be able to use all the features of our Web
          site if you do this.
        </p>

        <h2 id="sale-or-closure">If Beard Group is sold or goes out of business:</h2>
        <p>
          If we, one of our products, or one of our affiliated entities are sold to another company (in
          whole or in part), or if we go out of business or file for bankruptcy, your personal information
          will have to be given to a third party. By continuing to use this Web site, you acknowledge that
          this may happen, and that the third party who acquires the information about you may continue to
          use it in the way set out by this Privacy Policy.
        </p>

        <h2 id="changes">Changes to this Privacy Policy:</h2>
        <p>
          We may, from time-to-time and in our sole discretion, change this Privacy Policy at any time for
          any reason or for no reason. If you continue to use this Web site after a change to the Privacy
          Policy, it means you have accepted the changes we made. It is your responsibility to check this
          page for any updates.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 4fr) minmax(0, 8fr);
    align-items: start;
    gap: 2rem clamp(2rem, 6vw, 6rem);
  }

  .toc {
    position: sticky;
    top: calc(var(--header-height) + 2rem);
  }

  .toc ol {
    display: grid;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--gray-200);
    list-style: none;
  }

  .toc a {
    display: block;
    margin-left: -1px;
    padding: 0.4rem 0 0.4rem 1rem;
    border-left: 1px solid transparent;
    color: var(--gray-500);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.4;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      color 0.2s var(--ease-out),
      border-color 0.2s var(--ease-out);
  }

  .toc a:hover {
    border-left-color: var(--navy);
    color: var(--black);
  }

  .policy {
    max-width: 46rem;
    color: var(--gray-700);
  }

  .policy p {
    margin-top: 0.85rem;
  }

  .policy .policy__intro {
    margin-top: 0;
    color: var(--black);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
  }

  .policy a {
    color: var(--navy);
  }

  .policy h2 {
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    padding-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--gray-200);
    color: var(--black);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .policy h3 {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    color: var(--black);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.4;
    letter-spacing: normal;
  }

  .policy__summary {
    margin-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--navy);
    background: var(--gray-50);
  }

  .policy .policy__summary h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
    padding-top: 0;
    border-top: 0;
  }

  .policy__summary ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .policy__summary li::marker {
    color: var(--navy);
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .policy-layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .toc {
      display: none;
    }
  }
</style>
